Third-party software and asset notices

The desktop build emits a Third-Party Licenses directory with the npm package versions,
sources, SPDX identifiers, and original notices and license texts. In the app, select
About Fig Desktop, then View Third-Party Licenses.

The directory covers the Fig application code dependencies, the Electron and Chromium
download, the verified DeepSeek Harness npm resolution and pnpm fallback, adapted code,
and graphical assets and fonts. DSH and the pnpm fallback are obtained separately at
runtime. The DSH inventory records the preloaded resolution for the build platform.

The composer plugin contains code adapted from DSH Codex UI, commit 7b9f5e7, under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. See code/harness/composer/NOTICE and the accompanying
LICENSE-dsh-codex-ui. The adaptation changes storage to the host and rewrites the
client in plain JavaScript.

The Fig wordmarks embed Bricolage Grotesque. Fig also uses Geist Mono.
Their copyright notices and SIL Open Font License 1.1 texts are in
code/third-party-licenses/upstream/. The Fig icons and wordmarks originate in the Fig
visual identity assets. See assets/brand/provenance.json.
